@lostminds -- I have learned a couple tips for negotiating this issue.

1) ``layout_mode`` should never be exported to a file in the first place.  Don't commit it to your version control.  I kill the hunks in magit.  Knowing this is helpful because it effectively ends the cycle, though you have to watch for it.

2) ``layout_mode`` is only exported in the scene that the Godot Editor currently has open and active.  If you have five scene tabs open in the Editor and do Save All, just the one that's currently selected will save out ``layout_mode`` lines.  By opening a different scene, you can use Save All to save the scene you were just working on without generating ``layout_mode`` entries in it.
